read me

== Updating Extension ==

In order to update this extension for testing you'll need a clean venv with `Cython` and
then run the `cython` command to update the .c.

```
python -m venv /tmp/cython
. /tmp/cython/bin/activate
pip install "cython==3.0.12"

cd <repo_root>/test/demoappext-setuptools
cython --3str demo/ext.pyx
```

Run it from this directory so Cython sees `demo/__init__.py` and names the module
`demo.ext`. Use Cython 3.0.12 or newer: older output includes CPython's internal
`pycore_frame.h` header on PyPy 3.11, which fails to build there.

After those commands are run you can inspect the difference if you like.
